camchrome: the Windows anti-aliasing ladder on the Fontations backend; local() by full name.

Chrome renders Linux system fonts through Fontations (sktypeface_factory.cc makes them with
SkFontMgr_New_Fontations_Empty), not FreeType, so the coverage quantization of 1015/1018 never ran
for them. The Fontations scaler context now applies the same ladder (CAMCHROME_FT_COVERAGE_LEVELS,
which the browser sets for a Windows persona) to 8-bit glyph masks, in every process.

local(): under a cross-OS persona 040 substitutes the clone family ("Carlito") before the
unique-name lookup, and unique names are full and PostScript names. On a miss the lookup now tries
"<name> Regular", "<Name>-Regular" and the compact name.

Font-size stepping (the audit's text-scaler row) is not changed: stock Chrome on Linux shows the
same coarse stepping with text-rendering: geometricPrecision, so it does not come from hinting.

